WEBVTT

00:00.041 --> 00:04.963
The amyloid precursor protein,
abbreviated as AP, is processed

00:04.963 --> 00:08.675
by two enzymes, here
shown as beta and gamma.

00:09.217 --> 00:12.804
After cleavage,
amyloid beta monomers are created.

00:13.346 --> 00:17.142
Metals such as copper, zinc, iron, or lead

00:17.350 --> 00:21.646
can increase the expression
and activity of these processing enzymes.

00:22.022 --> 00:25.150
Metal ions are represented by purple
circles.

00:25.608 --> 00:28.153
The monomers form complex structures

00:28.153 --> 00:32.073
including oligomers and amyloid
beta proto fibrils,

00:32.323 --> 00:35.660
with metals aiding in the cross-linking
that forms a plaque.

00:36.369 --> 00:41.791
The aggregate leads to oxidative stress,
neuronal death, and cognitive decline.
